    "previous_model_response": "In right triangle \\(ABC\\),\n\n\\[\n\\angle ABC=35^\\circ,\\qquad \\angle BAC=90^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n\\angle ACB=180^\\circ-90^\\circ-35^\\circ=55^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThe matching arc markings at \\(C\\) show that \\(\\angle ACD=\\angle BCA\\). Therefore,\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{55^\\circ}\n\\]"
  },
  "answer_verification": {
    "status": "verified",
    "verified_answer": "35 degrees",
    "reasoning": "In right triangle ABC, angle B=35 degrees, hence angle BCA=55 degrees. At C, angle BCD is also 90 degrees and ray CA lies inside that right angle, so angle ACD=90-55=35 degrees, matching source GT."
